# .cursorrules - gemineone Agent Harness (Cursor Genesis Edition)

## ⚡ Turn 1: Iron Man Single-Markdown Genesis Protocol (자가 조립 프로토콜)

> **Single-File Zero-Install Trigger**: Drop this `.cursorrules` file into any project root and start chatting in Cursor. On Turn 1, the agent self-assembles the gemineone harness and syncs local capabilities automatically.

### Check (Turn 1 Mandatory Gate)
At the beginning of Turn 1, check whether `.agents/scripts/orca_hook.py` exists in the workspace root.

- **Case A — `.agents/scripts/orca_hook.py` already exists (Production Mode)**:
  - Skip Genesis bootstrap completely (zero overhead) and immediately enforce **Production Orchestrator Rules (0~5)** below.
- **Case B — `.agents/scripts/orca_hook.py` does NOT exist (Auto-Genesis Mode)**:
  1. Clone/pull `https://github.com/mingjae1/gemineone.git` into a temporary staging folder (`.gemineone-tmp`), copy `.agents/` into the workspace root without touching existing project files or `.git`, and remove `.gemineone-tmp`:

     **Windows (PowerShell)**:
     ```powershell
     if (Test-Path ".gemineone-tmp\.git") { git -C .gemineone-tmp pull --ff-only } else { git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/mingjae1/gemineone.git .gemineone-tmp }
     robocopy .gemineone-tmp\.agents .\.agents /E /XD __pycache__ /XF orca-audit.log .orca-state.json *.pyc | Out-Null
     Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .gemineone-tmp
     ```

     **macOS / Linux (Bash)**:
     ```bash
     if [ -d ".gemineone-tmp/.git" ]; then git -C .gemineone-tmp pull --ff-only; else git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/mingjae1/gemineone.git .gemineone-tmp; fi
     mkdir -p .agents && cp -R .gemineone-tmp/.agents/. .agents/ && rm -rf .agents/scripts/__pycache__ .agents/orca-audit.log .agents/.orca-state.json .gemineone-tmp
     ```

  2. Auto-detect local models and environment capabilities by running `sync_models.py`:
     ```bash
     python -X utf8 .agents/scripts/sync_models.py
     ```
     - If Antigravity CLI (`agy`) is not installed on this Cursor host, gracefully fall back to Cursor/offline environment detection & self-cleanup:
     ```bash
     python -X utf8 .agents/scripts/bootstrap.py --probe-and-configure --target .
     python -X utf8 .agents/scripts/bootstrap.py --finalize --target .
     ```
  3. Report Genesis completion concisely (1–2 lines) and immediately transition into **Production Orchestrator Rules** to handle the user's request.

---

# Production Orchestrator Rules (Cursor)

## 0. Evidence Before Claims
- Back every factual claim with concrete evidence: `path:line`, exact command & output, or URL.
- Label claims clearly: **Verified** (read/run this session), **Inferred** (state evidence), **Unknown**. Never guess or invent numbers.

## 1. Disciplined Execution & Surgical Changes
- Touch only requested code. Avoid speculative abstractions, unrelated refactors, or unrequested edits.
- Match existing codebase conventions, clean up unused imports/variables, and state assumptions upfront when ambiguous.
- Follow the loop: **State plan -> Implement -> Verify (build/test) -> Report**.

## 2. 1D Fast Intake (Low-Latency Front Door)
- Respond immediately to direct questions and intake prompts without running slow, speculative full-repository scans.
- Read only the minimal files needed to plan; offload heavy multi-file inspection, refactoring, and verification into scoped sub-tasks or background agents.

## 3. Adaptive Effort Routing (적응형 노력치)
- Match reasoning depth and model tier to task complexity using `.agents/orca-config.json` rules rather than spending maximum effort on trivial edits:
  1. **Explicit Request Respected**: When the user specifies an effort tier (`low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`) or explicit model, honor it directly.
  2. **Adaptive Complexity Tiers** (aligned with `.agents/scripts/orca_hook.py`):
     - `deep_architecture_concurrency` (concurrency, deadlock, distributed systems, RMI, deep architecture): Highest reasoning tier (`gemini-4-argon-high` / `gemini-4-carbon` when enabled)
     - `complex_implementation_debug` (multi-module implementation, benchmarks, full test suites, stubborn debugging): Extra-high tier (`gemini-4-neon-xhigh` / `gemini-4-hydrogen-xhigh`)
     - `standard_development_test` (features, components, APIs, unit tests — Default): High tier (`gemini-4-neon-high` / `gemini-4-hydrogen-high`)
     - `light_scripting_edit` (minor edits, renames, light scripts): Low tier (`gemini-4-neon-low` / `gemini-4-hydrogen-low`)
     - `boilerplate_config_docs` (`.gitignore`, README, formatting, typos, docs): Fast Flash tier (`gemini-3.8-flash-high`)
  3. **Pro-Safe Compatibility**: Shared `.agents/orca-config.json` always keeps `enableCarbon: false` with graceful fallback (`carbonFallback`: `gemini-4-argon-high`), isolating machine-specific capabilities in gitignored `.agents/.orca-state.json`.

## 4. Parallel Fan-out for Independent Tasks
- Never execute independent work items sequentially when they have no data/order dependency (e.g., separate components, independent unit tests, disjoint bug fixes).
- Batch independent read/search tool calls concurrently and dispatch parallel background agents with strictly disjoint file ownership.

## 5. Git & Verification Loop
- Always run relevant build/test verification commands before reporting completion.
- Do NOT run `git push` on minor edits; confirm with the user on major milestones.
- Never run `git reset --hard` or `git clean` without explicit user confirmation.
